 "final_text": "The proof is in place and `/work/mathd_numbertheory_314.lean` now compiles with no errors and no `sorry` warning.\n\nThe argument: 1342 = 13\u00b7103 + 3, so r = 3. Write n = 1342\u00b7k. Then n % 13 = 3k % 13, which for k = 1, 2, 3, 4 is 3, 6, 9, 12, so none of them is below 3. The first k that works is 5, giving n = 6710.\n\nIn Lean, I obtained k from the divisibility hypothesis, substituted r, and argued by contradiction. If n < 6710 then k < 5, so I checked each case with `interval_cases k` and closed it with `omega`. Nothing outside the proof was changed.",
